RADIUS-OF-CONVERGENCE NOTE (Paley T_7):
  H(T_7) = I(Omega,2) = 189;  alpha_1=80, deg I = 2
  smallest |root| of I(Omega,z) = R = 0.012514  (cluster series radius)
  => fugacity z=2 is OUTSIDE the disk |z|<R (2 > R=0.0125).
    partial sum_K c_k 2^k (K=  5) = 2.070e+10   (target log H = 5.2417)
    partial sum_K c_k 2^k (K= 10) = -1.080e+21   (target log H = 5.2417)
    partial sum_K c_k 2^k (K= 20) = -5.875e+42   (target log H = 5.2417)
    partial sum_K c_k 2^k (K= 40) = -3.475e+86   (target log H = 5.2417)
    partial sum_K c_k 2^k (K= 80) = -2.431e+174   (target log H = 5.2417)
    at z=0.05: partial sum_K (K= 5) = 157.24190521, log I(z) = 1.61293180
    at z=0.05: partial sum_K (K=20) = -42574384379.53292084, log I(z) = 1.61293180
    at z=0.05: partial sum_K (K=60) = -16535970427990044218980513653719040.00000000, log I(z) = 1.61293180
  CONCLUSION: the Mayer/cluster series is the ASYMPTOTIC/formal expansion;
  H = exp(sum c_k 2^k) holds as a RESUMMED formal identity, NOT a convergent
  series at z=2.  (Consistent with: lambda=2 is outside hard-core uniqueness
  for Omega(T) of max-degree >= 4.)  The EXACT per-tournament check that
  exp(sum c_k z^k) == I(Omega,z) as a power series is what we verify (0 fails).

==============================================================================
DICTIONARY (repo overlap defect  <->  cluster integral / virial coeff):
  b_1 = alpha_1 = c3+c5+c7+...  = |V(Omega)|     [IDEAL gas; H_free = 3^alpha_1]
  b_2 = -|E(Omega)| = -(p33 + p35 + p55 + p37 + ...)   [2nd virial = -excluded vol]
        p33 = #Omega-edges among 3-cycles = the 3-3 BLOCK of |E(Omega)|.
        (Full |E| also has 3-5, 5-5, 3-7, ... odd-cycle-pair overlap blocks.)
  b_3 = P2(Omega) - t(Omega)                     [3rd virial; cherries minus
        triangles of the conflict graph].  c_3 = b_3 + |E| ... (diagonal terms).
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A DIFFERENT (spectral) expansion -- do NOT conflate with the gas:
  TQ (tr A^7 = 7(c7+TQ)) and the Witt necklace cumulants W_k (THM-502/505) are
  cumulants of the WALK generating function det(I-uA)^{-1} = prod (1-u^k)^{-W_k}
  (Bowen-Lanford zeta of the digraph), NOT of log I(Omega,z).  They live on the
  adjacency matrix A, not on the conflict graph Omega.  Their only bridge to the
  gas is alpha_1 = c3+c5+c7+... = sum of ODD primitive-necklace counts (W_odd).
